  "crf": {
   "status": "NOT RUN",
   "implementation": null,
   "reason": "A CRF is a supervised sequence labeller and needs labelled training data. The gold set is 30 clauses / 88 mentions and was drawn as a test sample; training on part of it would leave ~20 clauses to fit and ~10 to score, which measures the split rather than the model. sklearn-crfsuite is not installed and is not in requirements.txt; pinning it would need the written justification CLAUDE.md §24 rule 5 requires, and that justification cannot honestly be written for a comparison that the data cannot support.",
   "what_would_change_this": "Of the order of 1,000 labelled sentences, which is a corpus decision (D-10) and an annotation effort, not a code change. The guideline and the scorer are both in place, so the labels could be produced without redesigning anything."
  },
  "transformer": {
   "status": "NOT RUN",
   "implementation": null,
   "reason": "Same data problem as the CRF, plus a compute one: neither transformers nor torch is installed, there is no GPU on this machine, and a zero-shot pretrained NER would predict PERSON / ORG / LOC / DATE rather than this project's eight labels -- so its output would not be comparable to the gold set without a label-mapping decision that would itself need validating.",
   "what_would_change_this": "A label mapping agreed with the team (ORG -> AUTHORITY, DATE -> DATE, and an explicit decision about the five labels no general-purpose NER has) would make a **zero-shot** comparison possible on AUTHORITY and DATE alone, without any training data. That is the cheapest honest next step and it is recommended in the implementation report."
  }
